-- 2026-09-23. Who sent an outbound message — the agent, or a person.
--
-- Founder-reported the moment the reply path first worked: "If a Human is
-- sent, it should not show the AI icon. It should show the Human icon, both
-- should be clearly differentiated."
--
-- He is right and the data was never there to do it with. `direction` only
-- says inbound or outbound, so a reply typed by a support lead and a reply
-- generated by Meta's AI were stored identically and rendered identically —
-- the same robot avatar on the same teal bubble. An operator reading a thread
-- could not tell which of the two had spoken to the customer, which is exactly
-- the thing they need to know before deciding what to say next.
--
-- NULLABLE with no backfill, and NULL means agent at the render layer. That is
-- honest rather than convenient: the Inbox composer shipped 2026-09-21 and its
-- first successful human send was 2026-09-23 07:25, so every outbound message
-- written before today came from the agent. There is no ambiguous history to
-- mislabel.
--
-- VARCHAR rather than a MySQL ENUM, matching direction/status/content_type on
-- this table: Hibernate maps these as EnumType.STRING and a MySQL ENUM would
-- need a schema change to add a value, which is a migration for something that
-- should be a code change.
--
-- Additive only: one nullable column, nothing else touched.
ALTER TABLE messages
    ADD COLUMN sent_by VARCHAR(16) NULL AFTER direction;
